@startuml UC-A1-sign-in-analysis-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-A1 Sign in (analysis: system sequence)
' Analysis level (decision 9): the person, Playground as one box, and Keycloak as an outside system.
' No route, store, port, adapter, token or cookie. Step numbers are the main flow numbers of UC-A1.
' Revised for decisions 10 and 12: the refusals, the second sign in, two tabs, Keycloak being down, and what each account sees.
' Logging (NFR-5) is not drawn: it is an effect of each message, not a message.
' Not drawn: a deactivated person is normally refused on Keycloak's own page and never comes back to us.

actor "Person" as P
participant "Playground" as PG #E6F0FB
participant "Keycloak\n(outside system)" as K #ECECEC

P -> PG : 1 ask to sign in
alt Keycloak cannot be reached
  PG --> P : "sign in is not available", no session
else
  PG --> P : 2 go to Keycloak
  P -> K : 3 prove who I am
  K --> P : 4 go back to Playground, with proof
  P -> PG : 5 here is the proof

  alt missing, used already, expired, from another browser, or an older tab
    PG --> P : "login expired", start again
  else the person cancelled, or Keycloak refused
    PG --> P : "login refused", start again
  else the proof fails a check
    PG --> P : "login failed", start again
  else the proof is genuine and for this sign in
    PG --> P : 6 you are signed in (this browser's earlier session ends)
    P -> PG : 9 ask for my account
    alt a pending person, or one Playground does not know
      PG --> P : 10 waiting page
    else a deactivated person
      PG --> P : 10 deactivated page, signed out everywhere
    else an active person
      PG --> P : 10 their page
    end
  end
end

== Every later request ==
P -> PG : ask for something
alt no valid proof of who the person is
  PG --> P : refused, sign in again
else
  PG --> P : the answer, once the account has been checked
end
@enduml
